    "lastDateReached": "2026-11-07",
    "why": "The single /events-tickets listing page has no pagination and no 'load more' -- it is a Webflow CMS collection that prints every upcoming show in one page load, and the last one on the page (Steve Lacy, Nov 7 2026) is followed by nothing. So the page's own end IS the coverage boundary: Moody Amphitheater currently has zero listed shows between Nov 8, 2026 and this study's May 31, 2027 cutoff -- that gap is real on the site today, not a fetch failure (it's an outdoor amphitheater; a fresh look closer to spring, when winter/spring booking usually firms up, would be worth repeating). The listing prints no year, only weekday/month/day; every date on the page falls Sep-Nov with no wraparound, so 2026 was assigned to all of them -- flagged here as a read, not an assumption, since the page's own event order and the 'this tour is happening now' framing make 2027 implausible for any of them. Ticketer is read from the homepage's outbound links (ticketmaster.com), not confirmed per-event since exact ticket URLs live one click into each /events/<slug> detail page, which were not fetched individually."
  },
